/* Perf A/B for the demo: big, soft shadows under the panes inside the pages (the Settings sections, the shop cards,
   the recipe cards, Home's event card and register, the Lucky Bag banner) and the dialogs' panels, made two ways.

   .be-filter-shadows: filter: drop-shadow(). It's the look a designer reaches for first, and the most expensive
   filter there is: each pane becomes an offscreen pass plus a Gaussian blur every frame, and the blur's kernel grows
   with the blur length and the screen's density.

   .be-box-shadows: the same shadow as box-shadow (6.7). It's geometry, tessellated like a border with a feathered
   edge, so it batches with the panes and costs about what no shadow does. It shadows the pane's box (with its
   rounded corners), not its silhouette, which for a pane is the same thing. Its blur is CSS's blur radius, twice the
   sigma that drop-shadow() takes, so 44px here matches drop-shadow()'s 22px.

   The tiles keep their hard shadows, which are geometry too (a thicker bottom border, --be-tile-lip).

   Settings › Performance › Blurred drop-shadows on panes, or Blurred box-shadows on panes (one turns the other off),
   or F in Play mode, which cycles none → drop-shadow() → box-shadow. The Performance pane is one of them, so it
   changes as you tap. Watch the perf overlay's frame time, the UI Toolkit Details profiler module (draw calls,
   batches) and the CPU timeline (RenderTarget.SetActive).

   Attached to the app root (BakeryAppScreen.uxml) so the two-class selectors outrank the pages' own rules. The
   selectors are explicit on purpose: filter: var(--x) where --x resolves to none throws in
   StylePropertyValueMatcher.MatchFilterFunction in some Unity versions (6.7 is fine), so the default (none)
   doesn't come from a variable. */

.be-filter-shadows .be-panel,
.be-filter-shadows .be-shop-card,
.be-filter-shadows .be-recipe-card__frame,
.be-filter-shadows .be-home__event,
.be-filter-shadows .be-lucky-bag__banner {
    filter: drop-shadow(0 12px 22px rgba(20, 8, 2, 0.85));
}

.be-box-shadows .be-panel,
.be-box-shadows .be-shop-card,
.be-box-shadows .be-recipe-card__frame,
.be-box-shadows .be-home__event,
.be-box-shadows .be-lucky-bag__banner {
    box-shadow: 0 12px 44px rgba(20, 8, 2, 0.85);
}
